<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' TA Bank eyes growing middle market.</title>
<headline>Philippines' TA Bank eyes growing middle market.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newly-opened TA Bank of the Philippines Inc will focus on the growing middle market, president Exequiel Villacorta said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are targetting essentially the middle market -- those businesses thinking of going public, going regional and even going global. That is our line of expertise,&quot; Villacorta told Reuters.</p>
<p>The bank is 30 percent owned by Malaysia's financial firm TA Enterprises and 25 percent owned by Philippine shipper Negros Navigation Co.</p>
<p>The other owners are Filipino and Malaysian individual investors. TA is opening its operation starting June 2.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
